  "description": "Contemporary Artificial Intelligence architectures universally serialize dense high-dimensional neural representations (h in R^D, D >= 10^4) into flat 1D token sequences. Under Shannon's Data Processing Inequality (DPI), this 1D Worm Paradigm inflicts irreversible information collapse, injects 140 ms quadratic decoding latency per hop, and incurs massive financial costs. POLYDIM / EinsofOS introduces a native high-dimensional computing paradigm where autonomous agents communicate losslessly on continuous Riemannian manifolds (S^{D-1} and St(D, K)) via Zero-Copy Shared Memory Inter-Process Communication (PMTP V1550+ and PMTP-v4 Triadic Fusion), achieving 34.8 microseconds control latency, 229.885 GB/s nominal payload-equivalent throughput on host RAM, 139.78 GB/s sustained VRAM throughput on Dual Tesla T4 / Triton SRAM tiles, and Neumaier compensated orthonormality drift <= 10^{-15}."
